---
source: tests/cli_help_snapshot_tests.rs
description: gpy-agent --help
expression: result.stdout
---
Fast, cross-platform agent for Git status and language detection used by the GPY prompt for Bash, Fish, and Zsh

Usage: gpy-agent <COMMAND>

Commands:
  start    Start the agent as a background process
  stop     Stop the background agent process
  restart  Stop the agent, then start it
  status   Show whether the agent is running, with its version and cache details
  theme    Export the active theme for the shell integrations
  oneshot  Render one segment without the daemon (the shells' fallback)
  config   Ask the running agent to reload its configuration
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Exit status: 0 success; 1 failure (one `Error:` line on stderr); 2 usage error.
status: 0 running (or busy); 3 not running; 4 not answering or unknown.
start, restart: 6 disabled by agent.enabled = false.
stop: 0 agent stopped afterwards, including not running.
